hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1644","**\nNarrated to us Baḥr b. Naṣr b. Sābiq al-Khawlānī: narrated to us Yaḥyā b. Ḥassān: narrated to us Muʿāwiyah b. Salām: Yaḥyā b. Abī Kathīr informed me: ʿAbdullāh b. Abī Qatādah informed me that his father (Abū Qatādah al-Anṣārī) informed him, who said:\n\nWe were once with the Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) when he heard a commotion. He asked, “What is the matter with you?” They replied, “O Messenger of Allāh, we hurried to the prayer.” He said, “Do not do that. When the prayer is about to begin, do not stand up until you see me. Maintain tranquility. Whatever you catch up with, pray with it, and whatever you miss, complete it.”"
